WHAT: build KIconEnginePlugin as a STATIC archive on WASI instead of a MODULE.
WHY:  `add_library(... MODULE ...)` means "a library meant to be dlopen d", and
      wasm32-wasip2 has no such thing. The link fails with
      `error: unexpected argument --no-undefined found` from
      wasm-component-ld while producing bin/KIconEnginePlugin.so -- an error
      that names a linker flag and not the actual problem.
      This plugin is NOT optional decoration: it is what makes
      QIcon::fromTheme() hand back a KIconEngine rather than Qt own icon
      engine, i.e. it is the entire reason an application gets KDE icon-theme
      semantics (theme inheritance, scaled directories, KIconEffect) instead of
      Qt simpler lookup. Dropping it would silently downgrade every icon in
      the app. So it becomes a static archive the application links and names
      with Q_IMPORT_PLUGIN -- the same shape the wk QPA plugin and the qsvg
      image-format/icon-engine plugins already use.
      QT_STATICPLUGIN is the define that makes moc emit
      qt_static_plugin_KIconEnginePlugin() instead of the dlopen entry point;
      without it Q_IMPORT_PLUGIN in the app has nothing to reference.
UPSTREAM: as-is in spirit. Qt own static builds do exactly this; upstream
      would more likely key it on `NOT BUILD_SHARED_LIBS` than on the platform
      name, which would be the better patch.
diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index ef464ec..700293a 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -99,7 +99,27 @@ install(FILES
   DESTINATION ${KDE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR_KF}/KIconThemes COMPONENT Devel
 )
 
-add_library(KIconEnginePlugin MODULE kiconengineplugin.cpp)
+# MODULE means "a library meant to be dlopen'd", and on wasm32-wasip2 there is
+# no such thing: wasm-component-ld rejects the MODULE link line outright with
+# `error: unexpected argument '--no-undefined' found` while trying to produce
+# bin/KIconEnginePlugin.so.
+#
+# This plugin is not optional decoration -- it is what makes QIcon::fromTheme()
+# return a KIconEngine instead of Qt's own, i.e. it is the entire reason an
+# application gets KDE icon-theme lookup (inherits, scaled directories, icon
+# effects) rather than Qt's simpler one. So it becomes a STATIC archive that
+# the application links and names with Q_IMPORT_PLUGIN, exactly like the wk
+# QPA plugin and the qsvg plugins already do.
+#
+# QT_STATICPLUGIN is the define that makes moc emit the
+# qt_static_plugin_KIconEnginePlugin() registration function instead of the
+# dlopen entry point; without it Q_IMPORT_PLUGIN in the app fails to link.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "WASI")
+    add_library(KIconEnginePlugin STATIC kiconengineplugin.cpp)
+    target_compile_definitions(KIconEnginePlugin PRIVATE QT_STATICPLUGIN)
+else()
+    add_library(KIconEnginePlugin MODULE kiconengineplugin.cpp)
+endif()
 
 target_link_libraries(KIconEnginePlugin
     PRIVATE
